# Issue #5610: a bulk append grafts its leaf over a range an existing leaf already
# holds rows in, without relocating them. The birth hint lies above those rows,
# so the bulk leaf starts past them unread. The fix relocates them into the bulk
# leaf at its birth, as a split relocates; refusing the chunk instead would fail
# a call that succeeds today.
MODULE: ReadPositionHonestBulkAppendDropsExistingRows
TARGET: ReadPositionHonest
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the bulk leaf is born without the rows the range already held
PERTURBS: Create

--- FIND
    /\ cache' = [cache EXCEPT !["a1"] = {o \in Offs : author[o] = PreAuthor}]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the existing rows are not relocated.
    /\ cache' = cache
--- END
